<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica money mkt shortage jumps to 10.37 bln rand.</title>
<headline>SAfrica money mkt shortage jumps to 10.37 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage jumped to 10.370 billion on Monday, the Reserve Bank said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The shortage stood at 9.556 billion rand on Saturday from 9.563 billion rand on Friday and 8.732 billion rand on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
